      "body": [
        "Apple's Hearing Aid feature",
        "got FDA clearance as the first",
        "over-the-counter hearing aid software",
        "",
        "A clinical study found",
        "self-fit users did about as well",
        "as those fitted by a professional",
        "",
        "Still, three things",
        "are worth knowing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "First, who it's for",
      "char_file": "무선이어폰_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "It's cleared only for adults",
        "with mild-to-moderate hearing loss",
        "",
        "Severe loss, and any sudden",
        "or one-sided loss,",
        "are explicitly excluded"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "If loss is severe or one-sided",
      "char_file": "무선이어폰_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "The software simply isn't",
        "built to handle those cases",
        "",
        "See an ENT doctor",
        "for a proper exam instead"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Second, what the test can't catch",
      "char_file": "무선이어폰_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "There's no professional",
        "fitting behind it",
        "",
        "You calibrate it yourself",
        "through an in-app tone test"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Fine adjustments can get missed",
      "char_file": "무선이어폰_illust.jpg",
      "body": [
        "Adjustments a real audiologist",
        "would normally catch",
        "can get missed",
        "",
        "An audiogram from a hearing",
        "professional works too,",
        "if you have one"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Finally, all-day wear",
